00:31:02.240 --> 00:31:04.760
- As a foreigner, you
need to look at e-waste

00:31:04.760 --> 00:31:06.600
from all that will
come into the country

00:31:06.600 --> 00:31:08.080
are second-hand goods.

00:31:08.080 --> 00:31:12.440
Cell phones, electronics, or
even very old cars, or whatnot.

00:31:12.440 --> 00:31:14.280
My brother, it goes beyond that.

00:31:15.760 --> 00:31:20.200
Go the Virius Albatois where
we slaughter cows and goats.

00:31:22.640 --> 00:31:27.640
We use ties, I mean car ties,
in burning those animals.

00:31:29.120 --> 00:31:32.680
And this is not a secret,
they don't hide to do it.

00:31:32.680 --> 00:31:35.680
You see them just look
for those old, used ties,

00:31:35.680 --> 00:31:40.640
put petrol on it, set it
ablaze, and put animals on it

00:31:41.880 --> 00:31:44.040
for us to turn it, just
to burn it with the fur,

00:31:44.040 --> 00:31:45.160
burn it with their hair.

00:31:45.160 --> 00:31:46.760
And this is what we consume.

00:31:46.760 --> 00:31:49.120
It is not solely for
the low-class, no.

00:31:49.120 --> 00:31:51.560
The ministers also buy
it from their char bus,

00:31:51.560 --> 00:31:53.800
and that is how they
skin their meats.

00:31:53.800 --> 00:31:57.280
It goes to the restaurants,
it goes everywhere.

00:31:57.280 --> 00:32:00.240
There's a day-to-day challenge
of eating what we have seen.

00:32:13.840 --> 00:32:17.560
(radio playing upbeat music)

00:32:28.800 --> 00:32:32.760
(speaking in foreign language)

00:34:38.080 --> 00:34:39.960
- This last week's fire,

00:34:39.960 --> 00:34:43.200
one of them was
going by the road

00:34:43.200 --> 00:34:48.200
picking the loose wires
and used computer stuff.

00:34:50.120 --> 00:34:51.720
So when he was going
around picking them,

00:34:51.720 --> 00:34:54.280
he was knocked down by a car.

00:34:54.280 --> 00:34:56.720
So he didn't die on the spot,

00:34:56.720 --> 00:35:00.240
but the lady who
knocked him with a car

00:35:00.240 --> 00:35:03.240
had to rush him to
our tingent hospital,

00:35:03.240 --> 00:35:05.120
which is a called a
moving tingent hospital.

00:35:05.120 --> 00:35:10.000
But when I went up there, the
doctors didn't attend to him.

00:35:10.000 --> 00:35:11.920
And due to that, he died.

00:35:11.920 --> 00:35:12.840
He died on the spot.

00:35:12.840 --> 00:35:14.160
I actually buried him.

00:35:14.160 --> 00:35:17.200
We had to send Pato instead.

00:35:17.200 --> 00:35:19.240
We had something that
we call tradition.

00:35:19.240 --> 00:35:22.240
So Pato still removed the
fingernails and stuff,

00:35:22.240 --> 00:35:25.760
we have to be able to
send him to the mother,

00:35:25.760 --> 00:35:27.920
who is the only
family in the north.

00:35:27.920 --> 00:35:30.920
The village that he
comes from is Sablulu.

00:35:30.920 --> 00:35:32.880
So we have to be able
to carry the remaining

00:35:32.880 --> 00:35:35.720
of the body to
Sablulu for the family

00:35:35.720 --> 00:35:37.600
to also see and believe.

00:35:37.600 --> 00:35:40.120
Because when they
see the remaining,

00:35:40.120 --> 00:35:43.440
they know it is true
their son is dead.

00:35:43.440 --> 00:35:45.240
Yeah, so because we
don't have the money

00:35:45.240 --> 00:35:49.360
to go to the necessary center

00:35:49.360 --> 00:35:53.160
where he was not taken
care of, and he had to die.

00:36:10.720 --> 00:36:15.400
- What I found is that,
if I went back to Africa

00:36:15.400 --> 00:36:17.520
and I found one of my students

00:36:17.520 --> 00:36:20.400
taking a laptop and repairing it

00:36:20.400 --> 00:36:23.960
by replacing the capacitor,
generating 700 dollars

00:36:23.960 --> 00:36:28.520
worth of value in
45 minutes of work,

00:36:28.520 --> 00:36:31.480
I would see the most exciting
thing I could imagine.

00:36:32.760 --> 00:36:36.280
And right now, the problem is

00:36:36.280 --> 00:36:41.200
that a hotel like this one,
with more than 1000 rooms,

00:36:41.200 --> 00:36:45.880
they replace televisions, the
big working CRT televisions,

00:36:45.880 --> 00:36:47.800
from hotels like this
around the country

00:36:47.800 --> 00:36:48.840
and around England.

00:36:50.200 --> 00:36:54.000
Thousands of working TVs because
their customers want flat.

00:36:54.000 --> 00:36:57.800
Somebody like Joe
Benson in London

00:36:57.800 --> 00:37:02.800
sees, hey, suddenly there's
600 working CRT televisions.

00:37:04.640 --> 00:37:07.120
He takes them and he sells them,

00:37:07.120 --> 00:37:11.320
and if you go there, you
will find those are not

00:37:11.320 --> 00:37:14.520
the TVs being filmed with
the kids in the dumps.

00:37:14.520 --> 00:37:19.440
The kids in the dumps have
some white monitor from 1995.

00:37:19.440 --> 00:37:21.160
That's what's being burned,

00:37:21.160 --> 00:37:24.720
but what's happening
is, people are reacting

00:37:24.720 --> 00:37:28.800
not to the color of the black
TV or the white monitor,

00:37:28.800 --> 00:37:30.880
they're reacting to
the color of the kids.

00:37:32.040 --> 00:37:36.840
And it's turned into a
bizarre racial profiling

00:37:38.280 --> 00:37:40.240
of the best and
brightest people ever.

00:37:41.880 --> 00:37:46.200
And this year, they actually
put a guy in jail for it.

00:37:47.520 --> 00:37:50.320
(dramatic music)

00:39:16.040 --> 00:39:18.640
- People like Joe
Benson and others

00:39:18.640 --> 00:39:20.440
engage in the same
type of business

00:39:20.440 --> 00:39:22.920
are actually doing
something very sensible.

00:39:22.920 --> 00:39:24.400
Because they're making
sure that people

00:39:24.400 --> 00:39:26.360
who cannot afford to
buy a new product,

00:39:26.360 --> 00:39:31.360
as he also said, can still
make use of this equipment

00:39:32.520 --> 00:39:35.040
and the equipment's
life will be prolonged.

00:39:35.040 --> 00:39:39.440
So he is a businessman, and
somebody using common sense

00:39:39.440 --> 00:39:42.120
would not pay for
something that is waste.

00:39:42.120 --> 00:39:45.560
If something is used, then
re-used, then re-used,

00:39:45.560 --> 00:39:50.000
and re-used, and in the
end, there will come a point

00:39:50.000 --> 00:39:51.880
where it does become waste.

00:39:51.880 --> 00:39:54.200
And there, he said,
when that happens,

00:39:54.200 --> 00:39:56.240
there's no recycling
facilities in Africa,

00:39:56.240 --> 00:39:57.680
which is also very true.

00:39:57.680 --> 00:40:01.440
The traditional notion
that the legislation

00:40:01.440 --> 00:40:05.960
like the Basel Convention
is based on is,

00:40:05.960 --> 00:40:08.720
to put it in a
simplified manner,

00:40:08.720 --> 00:40:11.880
that everything
that's used is waste.

00:40:11.880 --> 00:40:14.600
And the reason for
that is, as I said,

00:40:14.600 --> 00:40:16.280
that at the time
when the convention

00:40:16.280 --> 00:40:18.680
was negotiated,
in the late 1980s,

00:40:18.680 --> 00:40:20.840
you did not have
e-waste as a problem.

00:40:20.840 --> 00:40:23.440
It's not really clearly defined

00:40:23.440 --> 00:40:25.680
what is e-waste and what isn't.

00:40:25.680 --> 00:40:29.240
My vision, if that's not
too grandiose of a word,

00:40:29.240 --> 00:40:34.200
is really to see a world
where wastes become resources.

00:40:36.680 --> 00:40:39.360
(dramatic music)

00:42:14.240 --> 00:42:17.680
- Five years ago,
it went insane.

00:42:17.680 --> 00:42:22.600
Interpol created a thing
called Project Eden

00:42:22.600 --> 00:42:24.160
to start to arrest
all of the people

00:42:24.160 --> 00:42:28.280
who were importing
televisions to Africa.

00:42:28.280 --> 00:42:31.000
People like Joe Benson
and hundreds of others,

00:42:31.000 --> 00:42:33.240
and my friend Wahan.

00:42:33.240 --> 00:42:36.040
And that's where we said,
we've gotta get active.

00:42:36.040 --> 00:42:39.440
We formed an association,
Fair Trade Recycling,

00:42:39.440 --> 00:42:43.680
to try to create a network
in Africa's tech sector

00:42:43.680 --> 00:42:45.400
so that they can
communicate better

00:42:45.400 --> 00:42:48.280
to the regulators that
I used to work with

00:42:48.280 --> 00:42:51.120
and say, time-out.

00:42:51.120 --> 00:42:54.640
And the environmental
community needs to wake up

00:42:54.640 --> 00:42:57.040
to the idea of
collateral damage.

00:42:57.040 --> 00:43:00.600
That by raising
money in this way

00:43:00.600 --> 00:43:03.120
and telling ourselves,
patting ourselves on the back,

00:43:03.120 --> 00:43:06.960
that we're the great white
savior saving these people

00:43:06.960 --> 00:43:11.240
when actually, if you
arrested 1,000 Joe Bensons,

00:43:11.240 --> 00:43:15.120
if you arrested every
Wahad, you would do nothing

00:43:15.120 --> 00:43:18.760
to stop the flow of
material into Agbogbloshie

00:43:18.760 --> 00:43:20.840
that was important 20 years ago.

00:43:21.880 --> 00:43:24.600
(dramatic music)

00:43:30.360 --> 00:43:32.440
- The most harmful thing
is the burning of the wire

00:43:32.440 --> 00:43:34.400
because of the
dioxins and the toxins

00:43:34.400 --> 00:43:36.720
that were created from
when you burned off

00:43:36.720 --> 00:43:38.360
all the plastic
to get the copper.

00:43:38.360 --> 00:43:40.040
So I thought that was
the best thing to solve

00:43:40.040 --> 00:43:41.520
because it's the thing
that has the biggest

00:43:41.520 --> 00:43:42.960
impact on the environment,
and the biggest impact

00:43:42.960 --> 00:43:45.440
on the people's health
that are doing it.

00:43:47.000 --> 00:43:48.920
So the way the
system works is that,

00:43:48.920 --> 00:43:51.160
you put wires in the top
here, and then inside

00:43:51.160 --> 00:43:52.880
there's a shredder
that shreds it up.

00:43:52.880 --> 00:43:54.120
So there's a series of blades

00:43:54.120 --> 00:43:56.360
that spin around and
shred up the wiring.

00:43:56.360 --> 00:43:58.120
And then it comes out
of the bottom here,

00:44:00.320 --> 00:44:02.840
and it comes out as
lots of bits of plastic

00:44:02.840 --> 00:44:03.920
and lots of bits of metal.

00:44:03.920 --> 00:44:06.560
So that isn't a big mix of stuff

00:44:06.560 --> 00:44:08.800
that you have to separate in
two, which is the hard bit.

00:44:08.800 --> 00:44:10.600
So shredding up
wire is quite easy,

00:44:10.600 --> 00:44:12.920
you don't need anything
too technical to do that.

00:44:12.920 --> 00:44:15.160
But then, to separate the
plastic from the metal,

00:44:15.160 --> 00:44:18.440
you need to develop
another machine to do that,

00:44:18.440 --> 00:44:19.520
which is this machine over here.

00:44:19.520 --> 00:44:21.280
Should I bring it over here, or?

00:44:21.280 --> 00:44:23.520
(chuckles)

00:44:26.320 --> 00:44:28.720
So the way this device works is,

00:44:28.720 --> 00:44:31.440
that there's a pump that
sits under the bicycle wheel,

00:44:31.440 --> 00:44:33.080
and it pumps water into here,

00:44:33.080 --> 00:44:34.560
and it comes out
of holes up here,

00:44:34.560 --> 00:44:38.200
and it also causes
this basin to rotate.

00:44:38.200 --> 00:44:39.960
What happens is that
all of the material

00:44:39.960 --> 00:44:41.840
gets into the water,
but because the copper

00:44:41.840 --> 00:44:44.040
is slightly heavier,
it stays on this lip,

00:44:44.040 --> 00:44:45.880
and it's carried up the basin

00:44:45.880 --> 00:44:48.000
and through the
hole in the center.

00:44:48.000 --> 00:44:49.840
But because the plastic
is slightly lighter,

00:44:49.840 --> 00:44:53.440
it gets washed away, right out
of the basin and into here.

00:44:53.440 --> 00:44:54.720
So then you end up
with all the copper

00:44:54.720 --> 00:44:56.440
being collected
in a small bucket

00:44:56.440 --> 00:44:57.880
that sits behind
the hole, and then

00:44:57.880 --> 00:44:59.720
all the plastic ends
up in the basin.

00:45:00.760 --> 00:45:02.440
That's basically it.

00:45:04.240 --> 00:45:06.320
I'm happy with it,
as in, it's a system

00:45:06.320 --> 00:45:07.560
that's sort of in the works,

00:45:07.560 --> 00:45:09.440
but I'm not happy
in terms of the fact

00:45:09.440 --> 00:45:10.600
it hasn't actually
been deployed.

00:45:10.600 --> 00:45:12.960
It's not something
that's been implemented.

00:45:12.960 --> 00:45:15.960
At the moment, it remains a
concept rather than a solution.

00:45:17.080 --> 00:45:19.840
So the key is making
sure that money

00:45:19.840 --> 00:45:20.880
comes back down into the system

00:45:20.880 --> 00:45:22.840
so the person will use cycling.

00:45:22.840 --> 00:45:24.160
And therefore, they do
it because they have

00:45:24.160 --> 00:45:25.640
a lot more money.

00:45:25.640 --> 00:45:28.600
It will fit up to 30% more
money from the cycling.

00:45:28.600 --> 00:45:30.960
So I think, really,
you don't need

00:45:30.960 --> 00:45:32.560
to explain that
technicality or explain

00:45:32.560 --> 00:45:35.240
an environmental
reason for doing it.

00:45:35.240 --> 00:45:36.160
It has to be that you explain

00:45:36.160 --> 00:45:37.360
a financial reason for doing it.

00:45:37.360 --> 00:45:38.560
If you do this, then
you can make more money

00:45:38.560 --> 00:45:39.800
than you do at the moment.

00:45:39.800 --> 00:45:41.360
And I think that's how
you can convince people

00:45:41.360 --> 00:45:43.280
to use Assistant Miners.

00:45:44.680 --> 00:45:48.520
(singing in foreign language)

00:46:40.600 --> 00:46:43.520
